nd resuspended in 0.1% (v/v) formic acid prior to nanoLC-MS/MS mass spectrometry analyses. Tryptic peptides from the four conditions were analysed separately by TripleTOF 4600 mass spectrometer (ABSciex) coupled to the nanoRSLC system (Thermo Fisher Scientific) equipped with a trap column (Acclaim PepMap100C18, 75 µm i.d.×2 cm, 3µm) and an analytical column (Acclaim PepMapRSLCC18, 75 µm i.d.× 75 cm, 2µm, 100 Å). Peptides were loaded at 5 µl.min-1 with 0.05% TFA in 5% acetonitrile and peptides separation was performed at a flow rate of 300nl.min-1 with a 5 to 35% solvent B gradient in 180 min. Solvent A was 0.1% formic acid in water, and solvent B was 0.1% formic acid in 100% acetonitrile. MS/MS spectra were acquired by a data-dependent acquisition method involving selection of the 20 precursors giving the most intense signals, CID fragmentation with the Q1 quadrupole set at low resolution to improve sensitivity.\n'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
